id: pm-vcs-mhbz
title: Public git history embeds a personal author email and blocks release approval
description: "A full reachable-history identity scan found that every current commit stores a personal email in author and often committer metadata. The repository is already public, so fixing the raw history requires a coordinated history rewrite and force update, not a mailmap-only cosmetic change. No token, private-key, local-path, or LAN-address patterns were found by the current scan."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 0
tags[4]: do-not-publish,git-history,privacy,release-blocker
created_at: "2026-08-01T04:14:51.644Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T04:15:38.103Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: "Choose a public noreply identity; rewrite all reachable branches and tags plus audit unreachable objects; independently scan the rewritten object database and working tree; coordinate force updates and invalidate stale clones; verify GitHub, npm provenance, changelog links, and PR refs; document the migration without publishing the removed personal value."
severity: critical
component: release/privacy
customer_impact: Publishing releases before remediation would preserve personal data in every distributed clone and package provenance link.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-01T04:15:38.103Z",codex,"Immediate containment: replaced the tracked mailmap entries with name-only aliases targeting the GitHub noreply identity, and configured this clone to use that noreply address for new commits. Raw historical commit objects remain unchanged and keep this issue release-blocking."
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  .mailmap,project,current checkout no longer repeats the personal identity
tests[1]{command,scope,note}:
  git log --all --format=%ae | sort -u,project,identity inventory must contain only approved public addresses
body: ""
